class.description:
[UZULook] builds the U.ZU Engine look presets: a tuned [Environment] (filmic tonemapping, sky lighting, aerial perspective fog, ambient occlusion, glow and a color grade), a sun with soft split shadows, three-point and lamp lighting, materials for skin, foliage, glass, water and lamps, and camera lenses. All methods are static, so tool scripts and AI agents can apply the look without the editor:
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var root = load("res://main.tscn").instantiate()
UZULook.apply_to_scene(root, UZULook.QUALITY_HIGH, UZULook.ATMOSPHERE_HUMID)
var scene = PackedScene.new()
scene.pack(root)
ResourceSaver.save(scene, "res://main.tscn")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
Node root = GD.Load<PackedScene>("res://main.tscn").Instantiate();
UZULook.ApplyToScene(root, UZULook.Quality.High, UZULook.Atmosphere.Humid);
var scene = new PackedScene();
scene.Pack(root);
ResourceSaver.Save(scene, "res://main.tscn");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Class defaults such as those of [Environment] are not changed, so existing scenes keep their look until a preset is applied.
